//! Graph orientation tools.

pub(in crate::operations::catalog) const GRAPH_STATS: &str = "Report graph size, relation counts, the evidence split, and build freshness for the active repository. evidence counts edges that carry extractor evidence; evidence_share is that split, and it is not a coverage percentage. freshness.state CURRENT means the loaded snapshot still matches the revision it was built from. It does not mean a new disk walk just ran. Pass include_capabilities to attach the compiled capability matrix. graph_age_seconds is wall-clock age.";

pub(in crate::operations::catalog) const GET_NODE: &str = "Resolve one exact graph node. label is a symbol label or the exact graph id returned by another tool. One match returns the node plus its incoming and outgoing degree. A missing label is an error, node not found. A label that matches several nodes is an error that lists up to eight ids; pass one of those ids. This tool returns no AMBIGUOUS candidate list. Use find_references or go_to_definition when you want candidates instead of an error.";

pub(in crate::operations::catalog) const GET_NEIGHBORS: &str = "List the direct typed incoming and outgoing edges of one node. label is a symbol label or an exact graph id. The seed and each neighbor are id, label, kind, language, and span unless response_detail is full. A compact row also carries direction, relation, and, when present, coupling and the call line. relation_filter keeps named relations. max_results pages the rows (default 50, maximum 500) and cursor continues that page. Test and classified neighbors stay out unless include_tests or include_classified is set. A missing or ambiguous label is an error; pass an id from the error text.";

pub(in crate::operations::catalog) const QUERY_GRAPH: &str = "Bounded BFS or DFS from exact seeds or from a ranked question. question is the phrase; query is the same argument under another name. Tokens rank nodes by label hits, then by how many tokens matched, then by score. A file whose stem equals an on-label token outranks a function that matched one exact label. seed_symbols and seed_files stay exact and are not re-ranked. mode dfs selects depth-first; omitted or any other value is breadth-first. Each node is id, label, kind, language, and span. Each edge is source, target, kind, and, when present, coupling and the call line. Call get_node for attributes beyond that row. intent (callers, callees, imports, types, why) biases the walk, and the word call in the question can set it. max_nodes caps the witness subgraph. depth, relation_filter, flow_direction, context_filter, augment_seeds, include_classified, include_low_signal, and token_budget further bound it.";

pub(in crate::operations::catalog) const GOD_NODES: &str = "Rank high-connectivity production nodes. Files, modules, constants, stylesheets, and ubiquitous type names are skipped. Each node is id, label, kind, language, and span. Rank prefers callers in other files. top_n limits the list. include_classified adds nodes the default view hides. This is a static connectivity rank, and it is not a runtime profile. Use hot_path_review for complexity times call fan-in, and perf_attribution when you have your own measurements.";

pub(in crate::operations::catalog) const SHORTEST_PATH: &str = "Shortest typed path from source to target. Each end is a label or an exact graph id. A label that matches several nodes returns state AMBIGUOUS, found false, role source or target, and up to 32 candidates. Pass a candidate id on the next call; an id still resolves. A missing label is an error, node not found, and no near name is chosen. When both ends are ambiguous, the source side is returned first. path_kind calls, dependency, or documentation restricts the hop relations. A mixed path is never an execution chain: read path_kind and is_execution_chain. max_hops defaults to 8 and max_edges to 4096. bounded_out with evidence_completeness INCOMPLETE means a cap stopped the search. found false on a complete search means there is no path. relation_filter, flow_direction, and directed further bound the walk.";

pub(in crate::operations::catalog) const GET_COMMUNITY: &str = "Return one community. community_id is the index from list_communities, as a number or a digit string such as \"0\". \"00\" is community 0. An empty string, a sign, a float, an underscore, or a negative is an error: community_id must be a non-negative integer. An index past the end is community not found. view subsystems (the default) is the derived directory projection; connectivity is weak coupling. The answer is that one community and does not include a communities array. max_nodes and cursor page its members. Omitting community_id returns the same list as list_communities. resolution and hub_degree tune the subsystem cut; include_non_product keeps non-product nodes.";

pub(in crate::operations::catalog) const LIST_COMMUNITIES: &str = "List derived subsystems by default, or weak coupling when view is connectivity. Each row carries community_id for get_community. top_n limits the communities (default 20) and also limits boundaries to edges that touch the returned communities. boundaries_total and boundaries_truncated report the cut. resolution defaults to 2 and hub_degree defaults to 3; both must be at least 1. include_non_product keeps test and generated nodes in the projection. This is a clustering of the graph. Use module_map for folders and build_graph for package workspaces.";

pub(in crate::operations::catalog) const MODULE_MAP: &str = "Production folder map at one directory depth. depth is 1 to 8 and defaults to 1, which is the top-level folders. top_n caps the modules. include_non_product includes test and other non-product trees. The rows are directories and the files in them. They are not communities and not package workspaces. Use list_communities for coupled subsystems and build_graph for manifests.";

pub(in crate::operations::catalog) const BUILD_GRAPH: &str = "Workspace, target, and runner topology from manifest and lockfile evidence. No build tool is executed. Omit max_members for full member records, still capped at 500 members, 16 targets, 32 dependencies, and 24 modules. Pass max_members (1 to 2000) to set that member cap and to shorten each shown member to 4 targets, 8 dependencies, and 4 modules, dropping condition trees. Tasks stay full objects and are capped at 50. internal_dependencies stay as stored. status is INCOMPLETE when a cap drops rows, capture is incomplete, or diagnostics are present. The same typed model feeds architecture_inventory. Runners are capped at 200.";
